The '''Varrock Sewers''' are a network of tunnels under the city of [[Varrock]]. It is a fairly large [[multi-combat]] underground area filled with low to mid-level [[monster]]s and is one of the largest [[dungeons]] in [[free-to-play]].

A [[knife]], [[slashing weapon]], or sharp-object (e.g. [[scimitar]]) is required to access certain parts of the sewer to cut a spider [[web]] ('''note:''' a [[throwing knife]] '''will not''' work).

The [[dwarf multicannon]] '''can''' be used here, making it a decent place to farm [[Mossy key|mossy keys]] outside of the [[Wilderness]].

==Transportation==
The Varrock Sewers can be accessed via a [[manhole]] just east of [[Varrock Palace]]. Members can also access the sewers through [[Edgeville Dungeon]] by using a pipe shortcut near [[Vannaka]] - this requires 51 [[Agility]], and drops players off near some of the moss giants.

A [[giantsoul amulet]] can be used to teleport directly into the sewers, in front of [[Bryophyta's lair]].

==Features==
The dungeon is fairly popular on free worlds, as players may battle [[moss giant]]s which are often trained on. The dungeon is a multi-combat area, so low levelled players should bring extra food in the event that multiple monsters attack them.

The dungeon is also home to two bosses; [[Bryophyta]], a moss giantess boss, and [[Scurrius]], a rat king boss. To access Bryophyta's chamber for the first time, the player must use a [[mossy key]]. Subsequent visits do not require a key. Scurrius can be found upon entering the sewers and going east; he is a members-only boss.

Players can talk to [[Grimesquit]] on the south side of the sewers to start the [[Ratcatchers]] quest.

